Description: A compositor on another GPU, the application menu's 3D Video and 3D Display, a WebRender blob panic (ORDER 465)
 A hybrid machine routed the browser to the NVIDIA GPU while Stereo KWin renders on the AMD one: the layers' buffers
 (exported EGLImages) and hardware decoded pictures carried modifiers that are in none of the compositor's linux-dmabuf
 feedback tranches and KWin closed the connection ("importing the supplied dmabufs failed"). A frame whose
 (fourcc, modifier) the compositor does not advertise is copied to shared memory (render layers) or drawn into a
 render layer (decoded pictures); a pair it advertises stays zero-copy. The application menu gets 3D Video and
 3D Display, acting on the page's main video, for pages that take the right click. WebRender: blob images deleted
 later in the same transaction are no longer rasterised (Mozilla bug 1839001, Glenn Watson, mozilla-firefox
 6faf7d9af278), the "no blob image template" crash.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
